    "summary": "Model regenerated successfully after repairing the root cause.\n\n**Root cause:** The L2-1 model check (which independently re-runs the KG rule/code formulas against the built model) failed for the girder and both bearing lines. The formula engine was reading a girder count of **4** (the schema-default value), while the accepted decisions had been correctly computed from the description's **3 girders per span**. This made the recomputed values inconsistent with the accepted ones for every count-dependent quantity:\n- MR-02: girder.A = A_single × n_girders (3.417 with n=3 vs 4.556 with n=4)\n- MR-04/JTG3362-8.7: bearing count (6 vs 8) and hence Kv, Kh.\n\n**Repair:** Re-wrote the instance (`girder.count_per_span = 3`), which committed the true count that the formula engine reads. The formulas then re-ran with n_girders = 3 and count = 6, exactly matching the accepted decisions and the bridge description. No decision values needed to change — they were already correct; only the instance input driving the L2 re-computation was stale.\n\n**Final model (spine_beam_2d, simply_supported, single 30 m span):**\n- Precast prestressed small-box girders, 3 per span, C40 (Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³); single-girder A = 1.139 m², I = 0.3549 m⁴; combined A = 3.417 m², I = 1.0648 m⁴; w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m.\n- Two abutments on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end × 3 = 6 per line, 300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers, Ge = 1.0 MPa): S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 1.8e4 kN/m, vertical/longitudinal spring, rotation free.\n- Live load: JTG D60-2015 Class II, 2 lanes, ξ = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN; impact factor μ = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.402 Hz.\n\n**Results:** first vertical frequency 3.402 Hz (next modes 13.49, 29.88 Hz); self-weight support reactions 1332.5 kN each; midspan self-weight moment 9994 kN·m; lane-load max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m. All L1/L2/L3 checks pass."
